# Configuration

Pontia reads its persistent configuration from `$PONTIA_HOME/config.toml`. `PONTIA_HOME` defaults to `$HOME/.pontia` and must be a non-root absolute path without `..` traversal.

After editing persistent service settings, apply them with:

```sh
pontia up
```

## Basic configuration

```toml
bind_addr = "127.0.0.1:8080"
external_api_token = "replace-with-a-long-secret"
run_migrations = true
default_client_type = "pi"

[runtime.pi]
tui_command = "pi"

[workspace_browser]
roots = [
  { root_id = "projects", label = "Projects", path = "/home/me/projects" }
]
```

| Key | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `bind_addr` | Local HTTP listen address; defaults to `127.0.0.1:8080` |
| `external_api_token` | Bearer token required by the local Dashboard and External API |
| `run_migrations` | Whether `pontiad` applies its bundled database migrations; defaults to `true` |
| `default_client_type` | Default Client identifier; the current supported value is `pi` |
| `dashboard.source` | Local Dashboard build directory or remote `.tar.gz`, `.tgz`, or `.zip` archive containing exactly one `index.html` |
| `runtime.pi.tui_command` | pi executable or command used for launched pi Sessions |
| `workspace_browser.roots` | Directories the Dashboard may browse to activate Workspaces |

The release default for `dashboard.source` is the Dashboard archive matching the installed Pontia version. Remote Dashboard archives are cached under `$PONTIA_HOME/cache/dashboard`; an existing cache can still be served if refresh fails.

## File picker

The file picker powers `@` suggestions inside an active Workspace:

```toml
[file_picker]
enabled = true
min_query_chars = 0
max_results = 100
max_candidates = 100000
timeout_ms = 1500
respect_gitignore = true
respect_ignore_files = true
respect_git_exclude = true
include_hidden = false
follow_symlinks = false
ignore_globs = [
  ".git/**",
  "node_modules/**",
  "target/**",
  "dist/**",
  "build/**",
  ".svelte-kit/**",
  ".next/**"
]
```

Set `follow_symlinks = true` to include accessible symlink targets in searches, including targets outside the visible directory tree.

## Environment overrides

The running process accepts these overrides:

| Variable | Overrides |
| --- | --- |
| `PONTIA_HOME` | State and configuration directory |
| `PONTIA_EXTERNAL_API_TOKEN` | `external_api_token` |
| `PONTIA_RUN_MIGRATIONS` | `run_migrations` |
| `PONTIA_DEFAULT_CLIENT_TYPE` | `default_client_type` |
| `PONTIA_WORKSPACE_ROOTS` | Workspace roots as `root_id|label|path` entries separated by semicolons |
| `PONTIA_DASHBOARD_SOURCE` | `dashboard.source`; an empty value disables Dashboard serving |
| `PONTIA_PI_TUI_COMMAND` | `runtime.pi.tui_command`; an empty value clears it |
| `PONTIA_AUTH_ORIGIN` | Pontia Cloud HTTPS origin; intended for controlled deployments and development |

Environment values take precedence over file values for the running process. For persistent service configuration, use `config.toml`. The installed service stores `PONTIA_HOME`, `PONTIA_AUTH_ORIGIN`, and the required Agent Client paths separately.

Boolean environment values accept `1`, `true`, `yes`, or `on`, and `0`, `false`, `no`, or `off`.

## State files

The default state directory contains sensitive and durable data:

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `config.toml` | Persistent service configuration and local API token |
| `auth.json` | Pontia Cloud CLI credential |
| `e2e-identity.json` | Remote device identity private key and key version |
| `data/pontia-e1.db` | Local control-plane database |
| `workflows/` | Workflow Handoffs, accepted definitions, and Patch documents |
| `state/` | Runtime sockets, launch files, and integration logs |
| `cache/dashboard/` | Cached remote Dashboard bundle |

Keep the state directory private and protect its backups as described in [Security](/docs/security). Use [Device management](/docs/device-management) to rotate or revoke remote credentials.
